WEBVTT

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:23.840
<b>We're about to open!</b>

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:23.840
Today's specials: "Juicy Kara-Age"

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:33.030
<b>Juicy Kara-Age</b>

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.800
Full speed ahead!

00:00:33.030 --> 00:01:06.330
What was the dish that stopped the
commander known as the "Devil" in his tracks?!

00:00:33.030 --> 00:10:28.020
<b>Episode 2 "Juicy Kara-Age"</b>

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.800
I want you to be running like you mean it!

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.500
Stop lazing about!

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.290
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company commander of the Aitheria 
palace guard, known as the "Devil"</b>

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.370
You really think you can survive 
on the battlefield like that?

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.290
Another round!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.950
It's gotten seriously cold this year.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.300
A perfect day for getting some booze.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.450
Right...

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.820
Nothing like some ale 
after you've been running!

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.520
<i>This sucks.</i>

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.660
<i>I can't believe I am taking 
the company commander.</i>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.030
<i>I bet he'll love it there.</i>

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.310
We're still not there, Hans?

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.330
We are here, company commander, sir.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.000
Tonight, we're done with formalities.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.270
Don't be so stiff, man.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.700
So this is that rumored place.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.070
This is our battlefield.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.340
Let us go forth!

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.140
Welcome!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.080
Welcome.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.080
<i>Looks like a small but clean place.</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:28.950
We'll take two whatsontap!

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.690
Coming up.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.990
What's on what now?

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.720
Whatsontap. It's that famous ale!

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.490
Two draft beers, coming right up.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.060
<b>Whatsontap
THE thing to drink after work</b>

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:40.930
What?

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.600
This is chilled ale.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.070
Chilled ale, in this cold season?

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.140
It's actually great.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.540
Let's toast, company comm— I mean...

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.910
Berthold-san.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.210
Prosit!

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.230
Enjoy!

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.370
<b>Fizz</b>

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.240
That is delicious!

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.480
It's not anything like the ale 
they serve in other places.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.580
Right?

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.280
And then, they have this snack.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:23.290
These boiled beans really 
go well with the whatsontap!

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.460
<b>Pop</b>

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:31.560
<b>Pop</b>

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.630
Didn't I tell you?

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.800
<i>It's good, but it's too soon 
to fully accept this place.</i>

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.340
<i>On the battlefield, drawing careless 
conclusions will lead to your downfall.</i>

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.810
<i>But! I can't read this menu at all!</i>

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.610
Taishou!

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.480
Can we get some surume?

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.380
Coming right up.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.820
Taishou, that can't possibly be...

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.020
It's dried cuttlefish.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.090
It's good.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.930
<i>I came all the way here for a squid?</i>

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.300
<i>Tactical retreat is an absolutely 
legitimate strategy!</i>

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.400
I'm going to have something else.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.170
Please ask for whatever you like.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.500
I can prepare you just about anything.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.270
Very well.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.180
Taishou, I am a fan of chicken.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.280
I'd like some kind of chicken dish 
that fits this whatsontap perfectly.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:26.880
Berthold-san, that's certainly a tall 
order. Something tasty with chicken!

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.150
That's why I asked.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.590
<i>Chickens are a valuable egg-laying resource.</i>

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.420
<i>That's why the only chicken meat available is</i>

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.560
<i>the meat of old chickens 
that can no longer lay eggs.</i>

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.600
<i>This is nothing less than a 
trial that the hero has to face.</i>

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:45.500
Please have this while you 
wait. It's on the house.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:50.780
<b>Nobu's Specialty 
Whole pickled cucumber</b>

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:50.780
<b>Crunchy and tasty, you won't be 
able to stop eating this cucumber</b>

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.570
A plain cucumber?

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:50.780
It's been properly pickled, 
so it's delicious.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:56.750
<i>Salty, no, delicious?</i>

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:54.980
<b>Crunch</b>

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.150
<b>Crunch</b>

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:57.780
<b>Crunch</b>

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:57.780
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:01.750
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:04.990
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:05.520
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:06.790
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:11.600
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:12.860
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:13.700
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:15.330
<b>Empty</b>

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.770
That was close.

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:25.080
<i>If these hadn't run out, I would've spent 
the rest of my life to eating cucumbers.</i>

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.080
<i>But this temptation is just too—</i>

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.320
Excuse me, can you get 
me another plate of this.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.550
And two more whatsontaps.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.190
An order of cucumbers and two 
draft beers, coming right up.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:41.460
See, com— I mean Berthold-san. 
Isn't this place good?

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:45.500
Yeah, but the all-important 
chicken dish is not here yet.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.670
Oh, no.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.600
Shinobu-chan, can you go buy some pickles?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.070
Pickles?

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.110
Ah sure, I'll go right away.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.240
Oh, but I'm not sure I can 
buy them at this hour.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:04.250
Rakkyo is fine, too. You can get those 
at the 100 Yen shop right there.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.750
<i>Rakkyo? 100 Yen? What 
are they talking about?</i>

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:13.830
Shinobu-chan, it's dangerous for a 
woman to be walking alone at this hour.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.260
I'll go with you.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.430
It's all right. It's right there.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.370
<i>What is that light?</i>

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:29.140
<i>I don't remember that kind 
of alley behind this place.</i>

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.140
<b>Sizzle Sizzle</b>

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.380
<i>Oil?!</i>

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.180
<i>Enough of it so that the meat floats in it?!</i>

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.280
<i>What a frivolous luxury!</i>

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:43.420
<i>No, no, no. I almost let my guard down.</i>

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.090
<i>I wonder how that tastes.</i>

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.560
<i>All right, let's see it, Taishou! 
Let's see what you've got!</i>

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.330
<i>Face me!</i>

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.430
<b>Sizzle Sizzle</b>

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.000
Why are you putting them back?!

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.670
Didn't you fry them enough?

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.310
This is a cooking technique 
called double-frying.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.380
By frying them at a higher 
temperature than before,

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.610
the outside gets nice and crispy.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.180
Enjoy, this fried chicken 
is made with young chicken.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.050
<i>Young chicken?! I've never eaten that before.</i>

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.460
<i>This is not a dull weapon!</i>

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.960
<i>The weapon he unleashed 
is a legendary holy sword!</i>

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.760
It's time to face off! Nobu Taishou!

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.400
<i>It's so good!</i>

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.170
<i>How is it this incredibly juicy?!</i>

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.970
<i>The outside is crunchy!  
The inside is fluffy!</i>

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.680
<i>And yet it's still got texture!</i>

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.210
<i>It's almost like the chicken 
meat is dancing on my tongue!</i>

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:44.520
<i>There's no way this won't 
be a fit for whatsontap!</i>

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.450
<i>This is an encounter.</i>

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.290
<i>Just like the hero and the princess are 
drawn to each other in knight tales,</i>

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:56.630
<i>this kara-age and the whatsontap 
were destined to be united here.</i>

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:00.000
<i>I see, Izakaya Nobu.</i>

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.230
<i>I understand why the soldiers 
are talking about you so much.</i>

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.670
<i>You have bested me.</i>

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:09.110
<i>One piece left.</i>

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:13.880
<i>If I eat this, this miraculous encounter 
with this fried chicken will be over.</i>

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:18.350
<i>The least I can do is to 
fully enjoy this moment.</i>

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.810
<b>Crunch</b>

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.350
<b>Fizz</b>

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.490
That was delicious.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:25.090
It was a wonderful encounter of destiny.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.830
And now I'll have this fruit for dessert—

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.230
Hey, Hans.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.530
What is it, Berthold-san?

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.270
That fruit...

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.640
Oh, you mean the lemon?

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:42.010
If you put the lemon on like this, it makes 
it fresh touch and makes it easier to eat.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:44.010
Wh-What did you say?!

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:47.910
It is so much better than 
regular fried chicken.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.780
<i>This can't be!</i>

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:54.690
<i>The encounter of the hero and the 
princess was nothing but a prelude?!</i>

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.290
Hans!

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:03.660
Berthold-san, no matter how much you 
growl, I won't give you any of these.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.160
These are all mine!

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.800
That's terrifying.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.070
Hans, you knew about the lemon 
and stayed quiet, didn't you?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.880
He practically defiled my favorite place.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.310
Me taking that kind of 
reparation is only natural.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.780
You are so petty.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:26.120
But there's more to this story.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:36.260
<i>Now that I think about it,
I can just order another portion.</i>

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:37.000
Taishou—

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.760
I found rakkyou!

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:42.270
Good. I finished my preparations, too.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:48.810
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.010
<i>That was freshly fried!</i>

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.510
Taishou, what's that?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.150
Chicken nanban. It's Shinobu-chan's dinner.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.350
<i>Adding something to the chicken 
that was already that amazing?</i>

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.290
<i>That ultimate thing is being 
used for something else now?</i>

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:04.660
<i>This is like...</i>

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.660
<i>Magic!</i>

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.030
<b>Chicken Nanban</b>

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.030
<b>Tartar sauce made with 
rakkyou is the key element!</b>

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:11.860
<i>What a fool I was for allowing myself to be 
swept away by the encounter with the princess!</i>

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:14.070
<i>The real battle is starting now!</i>

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.930
<i>Only if I eat this can I conquer!</i>

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.440
Thank you for the meal!

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.770
Sh-Shinobu-san!

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.040
I'm sorry, but could you—

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.810
No! Chicken nanban is my favorite dish!

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.180
B-But...

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.150
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:31.850
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.150
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:33.690
So good!

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.650
Taishou, your chicken nanban is the best!

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:36.650
Isn't it?

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:39.420
The rakkyou is gives it a nice flavor.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.490
Taishou! Please make me more fried 
chicken and this chicken nanban!

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.900
I'm sorry. That was the 
last of the chicken I had.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.900
Wh-What?!

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.740
<i>My final battle ends 
without an actual fight...</i>

00:09:55.170 --> 00:10:00.650
Oh, no. If he's that mad, I bet we're 
going to have to do extra drills today.

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:02.410
I'm not so sure about that.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.080
Line up!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:08.190
It's a bit early, but I'm 
calling it a day for today!

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:13.090
What's going on?

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.590
The company commander is busy.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.530
I mean he does have to go 
fight his final battle now.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:21.430
Taishou!

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.500
Fried chicken and chicken nanban!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:27.250
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:24.400
You bet.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.120
When you think of Asakusa, Sensouji 
and theaters come to mind first.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.380
<b>Asakusa</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:39.880
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.880
And this person.

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:43.050
Asakusa is great. It's always lively.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:48.560
That's because it's a hotly contested zone 
with places that have good food and drinks.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.030
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:52.700
Shall we have a walk through this Asakusa?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.460
Let's do that.

00:10:54.330 --> 00:11:00.470
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the 
bars here to find the dishes featured in "Nobu".

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.470
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.040
It's a crime.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.380
Showing you that kind of fried chicken.

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:07.580
Asakusa, fried chicken.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:09.980
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi.</b>

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.980
Ah, I can't do this. I can't 
hold myself back. Let's go.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.850
Leave it to me, Nagira-san.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.790
I'll show you a place 
with good fried chicken.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.720
A snack bar?

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.120
Isn't it fancy? But you know 
what's really good here?

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:25.860
Well, there are are many places in Asakusa,

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:29.470
but if you want fried chicken, 
you come here, to "Kokoro".

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.830
<b>Local fried chicken bar "Kokoro" 
~ Asakusa main branch ~</b>

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:29.830
Right.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.040
I'd like to have some of your fried chicken.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:35.140
Local fried chicken bar "Kokoro"
 Owner Tomokazu Kanno-san

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.140
What was it called?

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:37.140
It's in this kind of thing, 
it's brown, it's foamy...

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.480
How annoying!

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.280
It comes in this kinda...

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:39.810
A beer?

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:40.580
Ah right! That's it!

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:41.250
Certainly.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.520
Right, first you go for whatsontap.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.060
This is too good.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:52.920
I get it.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:59.160
So everybody knows
about fried chicken.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:04.300
But if you were to say, hey Nagira, 
when did you first have fried chicken?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.200
I have no recollection.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.610
If I had to pick one thing, it might be 
the tatsuta-age kind from school lunches.

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:14.550
The ones where you season it with soy 
sauce before battering and frying it.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:19.580
And in my head, it wasn't chicken, but whale.

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.190
Uh huh. I know what you mean.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:23.320
Our pride and joy,
 "Addictive Fried Chicken".

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:27.790
<b>Addictive Fried Chicken
 The secret sauce contributes a rich flavor which 
brings the chicken's own umami to the foreground.
 The outside is crunchy, the inside juicy and tender. An exquisite dish.</b>

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.420
Look at that!

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:27.360
This is it, Addictive Fried Chicken. Nice!

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.400
So? How is it?

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.830
Well seasoned.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.570
Nice saltiness.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:39.600
In the end,

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.470
it's about the underlying flavor.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:49.010
I'm amazed that you can massage 
this much flavor in so quickly.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:52.320
You're right, we've made the sauce in 
a way that it's got a strong flavor,

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:55.250
so just a little massaging 
will transfer a lot of flavor.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.250
This is good.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.290
It's not a flavor you 
could experience at home.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:03.560
I know, this is something you 
can only enjoy at a specialist!

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.400
This is great.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.530
Thank you.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:12.200
Oh man, fried chicken and 
beer. A match made in heaven!

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.400
How about you?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.240
I bet you want to go for some 
fried chicken and beer, right?

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.380
I do!

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.580
I understand. I was in your 
shoes just a moment ago.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:26.080
Even Nagira-san approves of this 
"Local fried chicken bar Kokoro"

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.920
It's a five minute walk from Asakusa station.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:29.060
